# LF everywhere, because this repo's files are WRITTEN with LF on purpose.
#
# render.py, the tools and the tests all pass newline="\n" explicitly, so a page
# lands LF whatever machine built it - and CI, which builds the live site, is Linux.
# On Charlie's Windows laptop `core.autocrlf` is true globally, so git expects CRLF
# in the working tree and reports every generated page as modified the moment the
# renderer runs. Measured 03/09/2026: 34 files "modified" with an empty `git diff`
# and zero numstat lines. Two sessions in a row have had to work out that the churn
# was nothing, and one of them discarded it with a `git checkout` that also took
# real uncommitted work with it.
#
# Declaring it here settles it per repo rather than per machine, so a second clone
# or a new laptop behaves the same way without anyone setting a global.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so nothing normalises them. The portraits and icons are the whole reason
# to be explicit: a line-ending pass over a JPEG corrupts it silently.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
